%description:
ErrorModelBase: corruptionMode chunk needs a bit error rate

Ieee80211NistErrorModel computes a packet error rate from the SNIR but no bit error rate, so that it cannot corrupt a lost frame with corruptionMode = "chunk". The SNIR offset of -40 dB loses every frame. The error is reported by ErrorModelBase, naming the error model and the corruption mode, before the corruption is attempted.

Two ad-hoc IEEE 802.11 hosts, 20 m apart, multicast frames.

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
**.radio.receiver.errorModel.typename = "Ieee80211NistErrorModel"
**.radio.receiver.errorModel.corruptionMode = "chunk"
**.radio.receiver.errorModel.snirOffset = -40dB
include ../../lib/stochastic-errormodel-80211.ini

%exitcode: 1
%postrun-command: grep -h '<!>' test.out test.err > errors.out || true
%contains: errors.out
Error model inet::physicallayer::Ieee80211NistErrorModel cannot provide a bit error rate for corruptionMode = "chunk"; use corruptionMode = "packet" or an error model that computes a bit error rate
